  "sources": [{"title": "SENTRON PAC3200 Power Monitoring Device, Manual", "version": "A5E01168664B-04", "date": "2008-02", "url": "https://cache.industry.siemens.com/dl/files/150/26504150/att_906558/v1/A5E01168664B-04_EN-US_122016_201612221316360495.pdf", "note": "section 3.9, tables 3-6, 3-11, 3-22 and 3-26"}],
  "notes": [
    "Addresses are the Modbus offsets of the manual. Measured values and settings are read with FC03 or FC04; settings are written with FC10 and commands with FC06.",
    "Read every value from its first register with its full length: a read that starts or ends inside a multi-register value returns an error.",
    "The device ships with SEAbus TCP enabled on Ethernet; switch the Ethernet protocol to Modbus TCP first (offset 63015).",
    "The serial frame of the RS485 module is set at offset 63023 (8N2, 8E1, 8O1 or 8N1).",
    "Not in this map: the limit value, digital I/O and display settings (50025-50150) and the I&M data blocks (64001-64143), which must be read as whole blocks."
  ],
